<article class="env-example" id="05MW">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05MW">Example <span data-tag="05MW">8.7.5.10</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [dr]_{U} \ar [rr]^-{F} &amp;  &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \ar [dl]^{U'} \\ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> where $F$ is fully faithful and induces a Morita equivalence $F_{C}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'_{C}$, for each object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. If $\kappa $ is an uncountable regular cardinal such that $U'$ is essentially $\kappa $-small, then any fiberwise $\kappa $-cocompletion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ can also be regarded as a fiberwise $\kappa $-cocompletion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ (see Proposition <a data-tag="05MJ" href="/tag/05MJ">8.5.6.13</a>). Applying the criterion of Proposition <a data-tag="05MV" href="/tag/05MV">8.7.5.9</a>, we conclude that $U$ is flat if and only if $U'$ is flat. In particular, an inner fibration $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is flat if and only if its fiberwise idempotent-completion is flat. </p>
</article>
